{"name":"Stone Path","hex":"#e4efe5","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"},{"term":"path","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trail for the use of, or worn by, pedestrians.","A course taken."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a path in, or on (something), or for (someone).","To navigate through a file system directory tree (to a desired file or folder)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/path"}],"entries":[{"title":"Path (Toronto)","blocks":[{"text":"The Path is a network of underground pedestrian tunnels, elevated walkways, and at-grade walkways connecting the office towers of Downtown Toronto, Ontario, Canada. It connects more than 70 buildings via 30 kilometres (19 mi) of tunnels, walkways, and shopping areas. According to Guinness World Records, Path as of 2016 was the largest underground shopping complex in the world, with 371,600 square metres (4,000,000 sq ft) of retail space which includes over 1,200 retail fronts. In 2023, it was surpassed in length by Reso in Montreal. As of 2016, over 200,000 residents and workers use the Path system daily with the number of private dwellings within walking distance at 30,115."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Commerce_Court_Basement_Arcade_2021.jpg/330px-Commerce_Court_Basement_Arcade_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Path_(Toronto)"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/TunnelEatons.jpg/500px-TunnelEatons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/TunnelEatons.jpg/500px-TunnelEatons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Toronto's first public pedestrian tunnel under construction c. 1900. The tunnels connected the buildings of the Eaton's Annex.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATunnelEatons.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/LongosFCP.jpg/500px-LongosFCP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/LongosFCP.jpg/1280px-LongosFCP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/LongosFCP.jpg/500px-LongosFCP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Longo's market situated in Path. Use of the tunnel network as retail space began in the mid-20th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALongosFCP.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/New_PATH_west_side_Toronto_Union_Station.jpg/500px-New_PATH_west_side_Toronto_Union_Station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/New_PATH_west_side_Toronto_Union_Station.jpg/500px-New_PATH_west_side_Toronto_Union_Station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Work on new Path tunnels at Union Station, 2014","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_PATH_west_side_Toronto_Union_Station.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/PATH6.jpg/500px-PATH6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/PATH6.jpg/1280px-PATH6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/PATH6.jpg/500px-PATH6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Previous-generation directional signage for Path. Signs used a colour-coded system, with different colours representing different cardinal directions.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APATH6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/WPP-SS-1-WF.jpg/500px-WPP-SS-1-WF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/WPP-SS-1-WF.jpg/1280px-WPP-SS-1-WF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/WPP-SS-1-WF.jpg/500px-WPP-SS-1-WF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Path sign circa 2018. Current-generation Path signs list neighbourhoods and landmark destinations to speed na